# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.claude/

# TensorRT engines. Built by trtexec on this board and NOT portable: an engine is
# tied to the GPU architecture, the TensorRT version and the driver it was built
# against, and a mismatch either refuses to load or, worse, loads and misbehaves.
# Anyone cloning this rebuilds from the .onnx for their own machine.
*.engine
*.plan
*.trt

# ONNX exports. Intermediate artifacts on the way from .pt to .engine, and large
# (the detector is 82 MB). Regenerate with ultralytics' export rather than storing.
*.onnx

# Trained weights. These are the only artifacts here that cannot be regenerated
# from anything else in the repo, so do not just delete them -- but 44 MB of
# binary does not belong in git history either. Publish them as release assets or
# track them with Git LFS, and note in the README where a clone should get them.
*.pt

# Build and run logs
*.log

# Colour matrix refitted for local lighting; the default lives in receiver.py
ccm.json

# Calibration stills and the artefacts derived from them: hundreds of MB of
# full-resolution PNG, specific to one physical camera at one lens position --
# refocus a lens and they are worthless. Excluded by EXTENSION rather than by
# directory on purpose: the fitted cam*.json models are small, are the actual
# product, and belong in git, and git will not descend into an excluded directory
# to honour a later !negation.
calibrate/**/*.png
calibrate/**/*.jpg
calibrate/**/*.jpeg
calibrate/**/*.bmp

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Preview/inspection renders written by calibrate_fisheye.py --check and the
# capture server. Entirely derived; regenerate rather than track.
calibrate/preview/
